  "sentence_method": "one complete sentence per generation",
  "word_method": "independent word generation, not extracted from sentence audio",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "What would happen if you tried to blow a soap bubble in below freezing weather?",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Would it freeze and fall to the ground?",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Would you have to hit it with a stone to break it?",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "These questions came into my mind one cold winter day as I finished my freshly baked apple pie.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "It was a perfect time to experiment with blowing frozen bubbles.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "To blow frozen bubbles, I had to wait until the air outside was very cold, meaning 10 degrees below zero Fahrenheit or colder.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "I didn't have the bubble things that come in a bottle, so I used dish-washing soap.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "I chose a place out of the wind, and blew bubbles the same way I always do.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "Here's what I learned.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "If the temperature is low enough, the skin of the bubble frosts over, becoming cloudy instead of clear.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "And what about those rainbow swirls that you see in soap bubbles?",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "The rainbow colours stay even when the bubbles frost, but they don't spin any more.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "The bubbles still float in the air.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "They don't fall to the ground any faster than they would on a summer day.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "When these bubbles break, they don't turn into tiny drops of soap.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "They turn into shiny rainbow-coloured pieces and fly slowly to the ground.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "Sometimes a frozen bubble will roll across the snow without breaking.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-17.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "If it breaks, it may leave a strong bubble skin on the ground.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-18.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
